From: WineDroid
Subject: [PATCH] wineandroid.drv: Share the clipboard text with Android.

The Android driver had no clipboard support, so text copied in Windows
programs couldn't be pasted in Android apps and the other way around.
The driver now implements the clipboard manager window (in explorer, the
desktop process that also runs the Java side): it puts CF_UNICODETEXT
that programs copy into the Android clipboard, and takes the Android
clipboard text into Wine when Java reports a change or the window gets
focus (Android only lets the focused app read the clipboard). The text
last exchanged is remembered so it doesn't bounce back.
---
